WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.488
When you come across a photo of your cat, do you reach out

00:00:03.598 --> 00:00:05.193
to stroke its head once more?

00:00:05.417 --> 00:00:07.345
Pawture is an open-source project.

00:00:07.565 --> 00:00:12.248
Give it one photo, and your cat can settle on your Mac.

00:00:12.458 --> 00:00:14.571
You still know the markings on that face.

00:00:14.791 --> 00:00:17.957
While your cat sleeps, brush it gently with the pointer.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.675
You might hear only a soft murmur.

00:00:19.696 --> 00:00:20.607
[a soft murmur]

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:23.010
While you work, they have their own plans.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:26.432
Mimi comes over. Baobao touches noses with her.

00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:27.957
When they get tired, they nap side by side.

00:00:28.208 --> 00:00:30.639
One photo can't hold all the memories you share.

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:33.326
But how much your cat likes company or a nap?

00:00:33.436 --> 00:00:35.090
You remember. You can set that yourself.

00:00:35.292 --> 00:00:37.746
To me, a digital afterlife for a pet means this:

00:00:37.856 --> 00:00:41.590
the next time you open your computer, there's still a place for your cat.
